const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the single biggest reason people buy Telegram Premium?",
    a: "The 4 GB upload limit and ad-free channels, in that order. Everything else is convenience; those two change what the app can actually do for you. If you send large video or archive files regularly, the limit alone justifies the subscription."
  },
  {
    q: "Does Premium remove ads everywhere?",
    a: "It removes sponsored messages in public channels, which is where Telegram shows them. It does not remove promotional posts that a channel owner writes themselves — those are ordinary content, not Telegram ads."
  },
  {
    q: "Do the people I message need Premium too?",
    a: "No. Features like larger uploads, custom emoji and animated profile videos work outward: other users see and receive them normally without a subscription of their own."
  },
  {
    q: "Does Premium give me more storage?",
    a: "No, and this is a common misunderstanding. Telegram storage is already unlimited for everyone. Premium raises the size limit of a single file to 4 GB and removes download speed throttling — it does not add capacity."
  },
  {
    q: "Is Telegram Business included in Premium?",
    a: "Yes. Telegram Business is a set of features inside Premium, not a separate paid subscription. An active Premium subscription unlocks the business profile, working hours, quick replies and greeting messages."
  },
  {
    q: "How much does Telegram Premium cost in Uzbekistan?",
